ystem extraction\n\nKey Findings:\n-------------\n\n1. **Firmware Identification**\n   - Vendor: Huawei\n   - Model: S6730\n   - Version: V200R024C00SPC500\n   - CPU Architecture: ARM\n   - Format: Encapsulated CC firmware with magic bytes 00 00 00 00\n\n2. **Extracted Components**\n\n   a) **rootfs_xz.squashfs** (117.9 MB)\n      - Offset: 41668 bytes\n      - Size: 123581704 bytes\n      - Type: SquashFS v4.0, little endian, xz compressed\n      - Inodes: 49\n      - Block size: 131072 bytes\n      - Created: 2024-09-28 10:20:27\n      - Output: $output/artifacts/rootfs_xz.squashfs\n      - Command: dd bs=4M iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes status=none if=\"$firmware\" skip=41668 count=123581704 of=\"$output/artifacts/rootfs_xz.squashfs\"\n\n   b) **rootfs_gzip1.squashfs** (7.8 MB)\n      - Offset: 123648804 bytes\n      - Size: 8111913 bytes\n      - Type: SquashFS v4.0, little endian, gzip (zlib) compressed\n      - Inodes: 118\n      - Block size: 131072 bytes\n      - Created: 2024-09-25 02:38:59\n      - Output: $output/artifacts/rootfs_gzip1.squashfs\n      - Command: dd bs=4M iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes status=none if=\"$firmware\" skip=123648804 count=8111913 of=\"$output/artifacts/rootfs_gzip1.squashfs\"\n\n   c) **rootfs_gzip2.squashfs** (7.2 MB)\n      - Offset: 135199940 bytes\n      - Size: 7491332 bytes\n      - Type: SquashFS v4.0, little endian, gzip (zlib) compressed\n      - Inodes: 726\n      - Block size: 131072 bytes\n      - Created: 2024-09-28 10:20:27\n      - Output: $output/artifacts/rootfs_gzip2.squashfs\n      - Command: dd bs=4M iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes status=none if=\"$firmware\" skip=135199940 count=7491332 of=\"$output/artifacts/rootfs_gzip2.squashfs\"\n      - Extracted contents: $output/artifacts/rootfs_gzip2_extracted/\n      - Contains: Python 3.9, SSH client, SSH keygen, remote plugins, etc.\n\n   d) **uImage_kernel** (2.5 MB)\n      - Offset: 142746844 bytes\n      - Size: 2524032 bytes\n      - Type: u-boot legacy uImage, Linux kernel\n      - CPU: ARM\n      - Image type: OS Kernel Image\n      - Compression: None\n      - Load Address: 0x008000\n      - Entry Point: 0x008000\n      - Created: 2024-09-28 18:20:27\n      - Header CRC: 0x3EA90A9D\n      - Data CRC: 0x798D6EDC\n      - Output: $output/artifacts/uImage_kernel\n      - Command: dd bs=4M iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes status=none if=\"$firmware\" skip=142746844 count=2524032 of=\"$output/artifacts/uImage_kernel\"\n\n   e) **uImage_ramdisk** (9.2 MB)\n      - Offset: 145271292 bytes\n      - Size: 9589877 bytes\n      - Type: u-boot legacy uImage, RAMDisk\n      - CPU: ARM\n      - Image type: RAMDisk Image\n      - Compression: None\n      - Load Address: 0x00000000\n      - Entry Point: 0x00000000\n      - Created: 2024-09-28 18:20:27\n      - Header CRC: 0x5190CFC0\n      - Data CRC: 0x813AB911\n      - Output: $output/artifacts/uImage_ramdisk\n      - Command: dd bs=4M iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes status=none if=\"$firmware\" skip=145271292 count=9589877 of=\"$output/artifacts/uImage_ramdisk\"\n\n3. **Additional Observations**\n   - Multiple LZMA compressed data blocks throughout the firmware (properties: 0x5D, dictionary size: 16777216 bytes)\n   - Huawei code signing certificates embedded in the firmware\n   - Filesystem structure includes: etc/, lib/, mnt/, usr/\n   - Notable binaries in rootfs_gzip2: Python 3.9, SSH utilities, remote plugins\n\n4. **Unidentified/Unextracted Components**\n   - Multiple LZMA compressed data blocks (offsets: 6532, 15228, 23924, 32620, and many more between 132MB-135MB)\n   - These appear to be smaller configuration or metadata files based on their uncompressed sizes (ranging from 70 bytes to ~6.7 MB)\n\nOutput Directory Structure:\n---------------------------\n$output/\n├── artifacts/\n│   ├── rootfs_xz.squashfs\n│   ├── rootfs_gzip1.squashfs\n│   ├── rootfs_gzip2.squashfs\n│   ├── rootfs_gzip2_extracted/    (expanded SquashFS)\n│   │   ├── etc/\n│   │   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── mnt/\n│   │   └── usr/\n│   ├── uImage_kernel\n│   └── uImage_ramdisk\n└── binwalk.txt                    (full binwalk scan results)\n\nNotes:\n------\n- All extractions performed using byte-accurate dd with 4M blocksize for efficiency\n- SquashFS rootfs_gzip2 successfully extracted to reveal filesystem contents\n- Kernel and ramdisk are in raw uImage format (no additional compression beyond uImage header)\n- The firmware appears to be a multi-stage system with separate root filesystems and kernel\n\nSkill Reuse Notes\n=================\nRecognition Signals:\n- File extension: .cc (Huawei firmware format)\n- Magic bytes: 00 00 00 00 at offset 0\n- Binwalk signatures: LZMA compressed data (properties: 0x5D), SquashFS filesystems, uImage headers\n- Vendor strings: \"Huawei\", \"S6730\", \"V200R024\" present in firmware\n- Structure: Multiple SquashFS filesystems with different compressions (xz, gzip) + uImage kernel + uImage ramdisk\n\nCritical Extraction Steps:\n1. Run binwalk to identify component offsets and sizes\n2. Use dd with bs=4M and iflag=skip_bytes,count_bytes for large payload extraction\n3. Known offsets for Huawei S6730 firmware:\n   - Main xz SquashFS: offset 41668, size ~123MB\n   - gzip SquashFS 1: offset 123648804, size ~8MB\n   - gzip SquashFS 2: offset 135199940, size ~7MB\n   - uImage kernel: offset 142746844, size ~2.5MB\n   - uImage ramdisk: offset 145271292, size ~9.2MB\n4. Extract SquashFS filesystems using unsquashfs for detailed analysis\n\nFailure Patterns:\n- Using bs=1 for large payloads causes excessive runtime\n- Recursive binwalk extraction (-eM) can create massive directory trees\n- Kernel version strings may not be visible with simple strings command on raw kernel image\n- uImage data size from header may differ from expected payload size due to padding or alignment","path":"/home/icsl/sothoth/13-secflow-service/image_build/secflow-app-firmware-unpacker/unpacked-demo2-skipfix/S6730_V200R024C00SPC500.cc/output/summary.txt"}}],"api":"openai-comp